# Domain guards

Use existing `Ensure` (and `DomainException` / `NotFoundException`). Do not add a second guard library.

Guards run inside Domain. They protect invariants, not API input. Application/API validation must never replace them.

- Do not allow invalid objects to be created.
- Do not allow an object to enter an invalid state, even briefly.
- Do not bypass guards with public setters.
- Value Objects validate on creation. Entities validate on their own state changes. Aggregate Roots enforce aggregate-level invariants.

```csharp
public static Product Create(string name, Slug slug)
{
    var product = new Product(name, slug, /* … */);
    product.RaiseDomainEvent(new ProductCreated(product.Id, product.Name, product.Slug, product.Type));
    return product;
}

public void Activate()
{
    Ensure.That(_variants.Count > 0, "An active product must have at least one variant.", "product_not_ready");
    Status = CatalogStatus.Active;
    Touch();
    RaiseDomainEvent(new ProductActivated(Id));
}
```

