# Organization

**Namespaces are plural. Domain types are singular.** Folder names match the namespace. The `.cs` file and the type stay singular.

```csharp
namespace Stora.Domain.Aggregates.Catalogs.Products;

public sealed class Product : AggregateRoot<ProductId>
```

| | Namespace / folder | Type / file |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Correct | `Catalogs.Products` | `Product` / `Product.cs` |
| Incorrect | `Catalog.Product` | `Products` / `Products.cs` |

Same split for every layer under an aggregate: `Catalogs.Products.Events` holds `ProductCreated`, not `ProductsCreated` or `ProductCreatedEvent`.

```text
src/Domain/Stora.Domain/Aggregates/{Subdomains}/{Aggregates}/
  {AggregateRoot}.cs          // Product.cs, not Products.cs
  Entities/
  Enums/
  VO/
  Events/
  Repositories/               // only when the interface exists
```

Namespaces match folders:

```text
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}.Entities
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}.Enums
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}.VO
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}.Events
Stora.Domain.Aggregates.{Subdomains}.{Aggregates}.Repositories
```

Subdomain namespace map (plural; uncountable labels stay as the ubiquitous-language word):

| Subdomain namespace | Aggregates (plural folder → singular type) |
| --- | --- |
| `Catalogs` | `Products` → `Product`, `Categories` → `Category`, `CatalogAttributes` → `CatalogAttribute`, `Brands` → `Brand`, `ProductTags` → `ProductTag`, `ProductCollections` → `ProductCollection`, `ProductReviews` → `ProductReview` |
| `Pricing` | `PriceLists` → `PriceList`, `Coupons` → `Coupon`, `Promotions` → `Promotion` |
| `Inventories` | `InventoryItems` → `InventoryItem`, `Warehouses` → `Warehouse` |
| `Customers` | `Customers` → `Customer`, `CustomerGroups` → `CustomerGroup`, `Wishlists` → `Wishlist` |
| `Carts` | `Carts` → `Cart` |
| `Checkouts` | `Checkouts` → `Checkout` |
| `Orders` | `Orders` → `Order` |
| `Payments` | `Payments` → `Payment`, `PaymentMethods` → `PaymentMethod` |
| `Shipping` | `Shipments` → `Shipment`, `ShippingMethods` → `ShippingMethod`, `ShippingClasses` → `ShippingClass`, `ShippingZones` → `ShippingZone` |
| `Taxes` | `TaxClasses` → `TaxClass` |
| `Content` | `Posts` → `Post`, `PostCategories` → `PostCategory`, `PostComments` → `PostComment`, `Pages` → `Page` |
| `Media` | `Media` → `Media`, `MediaFolders` → `MediaFolder` |
| `Messaging` | `Outboxes` → `Outbox`, `Inboxes` → `Inbox` |
| `Identity` | `Users` → `User`, `Roles` → `Role` |
| `Admins` | `AuditLogs` → `AuditLog` |
| `Settings` | `StoreSettings` → `StoreSettings` |
| `Notifications` | `Notifications` → `Notification`, `NotificationTemplates` → `NotificationTemplate`, `NotificationPreferences` → `NotificationPreference` |
| `Integrations` | `Webhooks` → `Webhook` |

Existing folders and namespaces follow this map.

Add a subdomain only for a real business capability. Do not create empty `Entities` / `Enums` / `VO` / `Events` / `Repositories` folders.

Shared types (`Money`, `Sku`, `Address`, `Email`, `Quantity`, …) stay in `Stora.Domain.SharedKernel`. Do not move aggregate-owned types into SharedKernel. `SharedKernel` is a technical folder name, not a pluralized aggregate.

**One C# type per `.cs` file.** No `Enums.cs`, `Events.cs`, or similar dumps.

