# Enums

Every enum member has `[Description("…")]` in **Persian**. Member names stay English.

```csharp
public enum CatalogStatus
{
    [Description("پیش‌نویس")]
    Draft = 0,
    [Description("فعال")]
    Active = 1,
}
```

---

# Documentation

English XML docs on Domain types, properties, and methods. Explain business responsibility, not “this is a class.” Identifiers stay English. Persian is only for enum `Description` values.

Existing files may lack per-property comments; add them when touching that type, not as a drive-by rewrite of the whole layer.

---

# New aggregate checklist

1. Business responsibility and owning subdomain
2. Boundary, root, entities, VOs, enums
3. Creation/modification invariants and `Ensure` guards
4. Domain behavior on the root
5. Meaningful past-tense events raised on the root
6. One type per file; namespaces matching folders (plural namespace segments, singular types)
7. English docs; Persian enum descriptions
8. Repository interface only when asked

Do not invent aggregates to fill folders. Do not introduce business behavior during a structural refactor. After any Domain refactor, the solution must build.
